.TH "DEDB IMPORT" "1" "2026-01-01" "0.0.16" "dedb import Manual"
.SH NAME
dedb\-import \- Create DOSEMU2 config(s) from downloaded games or dosbox.conf files.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dedb import
[OPTIONS] SOURCES...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create DOSEMU2 config(s) from downloaded games or dosbox.conf files.
.PP
SOURCES is one or more downloaded games ('gog:<id>' / 'archive:<id>',
an archive.org URL, a bare downloaded name, or bare ids with -b) -
each converted into its own dosemu/ directory - OR one or more
dosbox.conf paths merged (later files overriding earlier) into a
single config written to --output-dir.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o,\fP \-\-output\-dir DIRECTORY
Directory to write the DOSEMU2 config(s) into. For a game it defaults to the download's dosemu/ dir; for conf files it is required.
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fP TEXT
Launch profile to convert (gog only).
.TP
\fB\-b,\fP \-\-backend SCHEME
Read SOURCES as bare game ids for this backend, rather than dosbox.conf paths.
.TP
\fB\-f,\fP \-\-force
Overwrite an existing output dir.
.TP
\fB\-\-refreshconf\fP
Regenerate the config for an already-downloaded game (implies --force; skips if not downloaded).
